{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities","id":1193199,"title":"[BPG] Inguma \u2013 Family of Outsiders \u2013 and minorities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-08T10:43:06-08:00","id":1193199,"title":"[BPG] Inguma \u2013 Family of Outsiders \u2013 and minorities","content":"<b>BPG</b> means <b>Beast Player\u2019s Guide </b>\u2013 and in this book is new Family of Beasts. So called <i>Inguma</i> are embodying the idea of Fear of the Other in a given community. With rise of xenophobia ( and any other minorities \u2013phobia, in reality ) in my homeland Poland \u2013 and me writing fan Dark Era <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125616-fan-dark-era-conquest-of-paradise-age-of-explorationhttp:/forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125616-fan-dark-era-conquest-of-paradise-age-of-exploration\">Conquest of Paradise</a> </b>about 15<sup>th</sup> century Portugal and Spain in that were rise of violent actions against local Jews and Muslims \u2013 I wonder how much <i>Inguma</i> reflects those fears. As bisexual man I also looks for this Family also reflecting LGBT+ \u2018minority as monsters\u2019 in society Eye of Beholder ( pun intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). <b>Topic is for reflecting this kind character and try to use those Fears in not too much offensive way.</b> But still \u2013 as embodied by monstrous Horrors the unreal fears of humanity \u2013 some grotesque views probably cannot be missed. <b>Best would be pointing or things like Inguma Horrors could look like.</b><br /> <br /> For example, for <i>Conquest of Paradise </i>I was thinking about Horror reflecting antiJews views as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dybbuk\" target=\"_blank\">Dybbuk</a>, vengeful spirit from People of Torah myths. Or maybe Golem is good example of Inguma Horror? He would spread irrational fear in humans seeing him, not very different than this of Prometheans.<br /> <br /> <b>I have real problem in imaging how could look like Horror reflecting fears about LGBT+ people</b> - What, this being would look like mismatched amalgam of male and women parts? Or something like <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Slaanesh\" target=\"_blank\">Warhammer\u2019s Slaanesh</a>? Because \u2018man dressed as women\u2019 is clearly not enough as true Horror image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-08-2018, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:49:34-08:00","id":1193202,"title":"","content":"A hermaphroditic, goat-headed Satan-figure? An incubus/succubus that changes its gender freely and disconcerts onlookers by appearing as the gender they don't consider themselves attracted to and being attractive nonetheless (i.e. using Alien Allure and some variant of Enemy Within)?<br /> <br /> I dunno. I'm bisexual myself, so it's kinda difficult for me too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-08-2018, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:08:11-08:00","id":1193209,"title":"","content":"May a point out that there is a pretty popular movie classic in our community that is all about taking the absurd cishet fears about us to an extreme where we are predatory aliens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:34:22-08:00","id":1193222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193209#post1193209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May a point out that there is a pretty popular movie classic in our community that is all about taking the absurd cishet fears about us to an extreme where we are predatory aliens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Point me to it straight ahead - I need a good laugh just before my sleep. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What's a title?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:37:02-08:00","id":1193224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193222#post1193222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point me to it straight ahead - I need a good laugh just before my sleep. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What's a title?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rocky Horror Picture Show<br /> <br /> I recommend seeing it with a crowd that knows the call backs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:40:36-08:00","id":1193227,"title":"","content":"I think a Horror representing homophobia/fear of queers would not necessary manifest in some way iconic of being queer, but rather, would represent the myths that homophobes spread. Things like: gays are promiscuous, gays are diseased, gays prey on children/virgins/Good Straight People, trans people are sexual perverts, etc. So something like a diseased body with a prolapsed rectum and lipstick....which sounds ludicrous, I realize as I type it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, an Inguma Enabler might actually have a very appealing Horror...and they feed by getting homophobic blowhards to reciprocate a (seeming) same-sex advance. And then their Whisper broodmate takes pictures. ;-)<br /> <br /> (apparently this is the thread for bi people!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:43:13-08:00","id":1193229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193227#post1193227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Horror representing homophobia/fear of queers would not necessary manifest in some way iconic of being queer, but rather, would represent the myths that homophobes spread. Things like: gays are promiscuous, gays are diseased, gays prey on children/virgins/Good Straight People, trans people are sexual perverts, etc. So something like a diseased body with a prolapsed rectum and lipstick....which sounds ludicrous, I realize as I type it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, that strikes me as more Namtaru than Inguma. Inguma are about the fear of something that creeps into your life or your community and corrupts it from the inside, such that by the end no-one's willing to acknowledge that the corruption <i>is</i> corruption. They're the outsider, the pod person, the Reptilian. They're the Other (Wo)Man, the courtesan the king loves better than his wife but who just seeks to take advantage of him, the poisoner of minds and marriages. They're the new kid who turns the school against you. They're the orchestrators of betrayals, the Iago to your Othello. They're perhaps the most subtle and certainly the closest to 'civilized' of the Families, because they were <i>born</i> from civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-08-2018, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:48:25-08:00","id":1193232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193224#post1193224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rocky Horror Picture Show</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know about this as Inguma inspiration - Doctor Frank-N-Furter is <i>just</i> transvestite. He is not something <b>truly </b>inhuman, like Horrors should be. ( At least that was vibe I get from reading <b>BPG</b> now. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:52:55-08:00","id":1193235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193227#post1193227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(apparently this is the thread for bi people!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather <i>all </i>minorities groups - Queer are just most interesting topic as we do not have many myths about them as Fears engines, compared to whole mythologies of ethnics groups ( like Jews, for example ). Still, you are welcome here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:57:23-08:00","id":1193239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193232#post1193232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not know about this as Inguma inspiration - Doctor Frank-N-Furter is <i>just</i> transvestite. He is not something <b>truly </b>inhuman, like Horrors should be. ( At least that was vibe I get from reading <b>BPG</b> now. )</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean in terms of his physical appearance? Because he IS an an extraterrestrial, and having forms that \u201ccreepily\u201d masquerade as human is part of the horror shtick of the Inguma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-08-2018, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:24:15-08:00","id":1193250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193224#post1193224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rocky Horror Picture Show<br /> <br /> I recommend seeing it with a crowd that knows the call backs.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I thought you about to say Alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:18:30-08:00","id":1193280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193250#post1193250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here I thought you about to say Alien.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reproductive horror aspect undermines any attempt to draw straight-fears-of-LGBT-predator associations.<br /> <br /> Predator vs Alien though works quite well as a conflict between primal \u201cmasculine\u201d and \u201cfeminine\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:11:35-08:00","id":1193406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193227#post1193227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Horror representing homophobia/fear of queers would not necessary manifest in some way iconic of being queer, but rather, would represent the myths that homophobes spread. Things like: gays are promiscuous, gays are diseased, gays prey on children/virgins/Good Straight People, trans people are sexual perverts, etc. So something like a diseased body with a prolapsed rectum and lipstick....which sounds ludicrous, I realize as I type it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, an Inguma Enabler might actually have a very appealing Horror...and they feed by getting homophobic blowhards to reciprocate a (seeming) same-sex advance. And then their Whisper broodmate takes pictures. ;-)<br /> <br /> (apparently this is the thread for bi people!)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, it's the Bi thread. I think for the specific fear of 'Others' invoked by people who fear LGBT people you wanna go for body horror, but subtle body horror. Make it look perfectly normal until you really pay attention and catch the horrifying part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:22:21-08:00","id":1193408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193235#post1193235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather <i>all </i>minorities groups - Queer are just most interesting topic as we do not have many myths about them as Fears engines, compared to whole mythologies of ethnics groups ( like Jews, for example ). Still, you are welcome here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> , I was just commenting on how many posters (including me!) are bi, not implying that it was a bi-exclusive thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T21:23:51-08:00","id":1193424,"title":"","content":"Just because people should not fear it, doesn't mean they won't.<br /> <br /> The Outsiders may be the fear of the Other personified but that does not mean they have to reinforce those fears. They can easily be 'invasion of the body snatchers' horror as easily as xenophobia/homophobia/etc. Families provide tools and patterns but the manifestation of the fear comes from the Hunger.<br /> <br /> The difference between a Makara Tyrant and an Inguma Tyrant is in how they go about sating that Hunger, it is still ultimately about power. The families are the trappings, the colour, the excuse. The real fear is what they Hunger for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 03-09-2018, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T23:55:51-08:00","id":1193453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193424#post1193424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because people should not fear it, doesn't mean they won't.<br /> <br /> The Outsiders may be the fear of the Other personified but that does not mean they have to reinforce those fears. They can easily be 'invasion of the body snatchers' horror as easily as xenophobia/homophobia/etc. Families provide tools and patterns but the manifestation of the fear comes from the Hunger.<br /> <br /> The difference between a Makara Tyrant and an Inguma Tyrant is in how they go about sating that Hunger, it is still ultimately about power. The families are the trappings, the colour, the excuse. The real fear is what they Hunger for.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193229#post1193229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, that strikes me as more Namtaru than Inguma. Inguma are about the fear of something that creeps into your life or your community and corrupts it from the inside, such that by the end no-one's willing to acknowledge that the corruption <i>is</i> corruption. They're the outsider, the pod person, the Reptilian. They're the Other (Wo)Man, the courtesan the king loves better than his wife but who just seeks to take advantage of him, the poisoner of minds and marriages. They're the new kid who turns the school against you. They're the orchestrators of betrayals, the Iago to your Othello. They're perhaps the most subtle and certainly the closest to 'civilized' of the Families, because they were <i>born</i> from civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combaining those two responses - <b>So Family in BtP, in the end, is only 'Color' of PC? </b>The same archetype of Horror can easily by Inguma, Namtaru or Makara, depending only on players choice?<br /> <br /> <b>So what are most striking traits of Inguma on their own? 'Subversiveness' of community?</b> For example - Does ethnic mythological being inside the human body of the same ethnicity <i>is not</i> Inguma, as it's too much 'in the open'? First Nation Horror inside First Nation human is too much counter to Inguma inborn 'stealthiness' inside population? Would Dybbuk inside Jew person is not good for Inguma Family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-09-2018, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T00:30:51-08:00","id":1193460,"title":"","content":"I didn't quite get the last questions, but from my understanding:<br /> Inguma are the Fear of the Other, Makara the Fear of Drowning and Namtaru the Fear of Revulsion. The same Archetype of Horror can easily be either of those, depending on where you put your focus. Is it more about fearing something because it is different, or because it makes you gag? Former Inguma, later Namtaru.<br /> Other example: Is the Dragon scary because you're powerless to fight it, or because you're defenseless ('exposed') against this monster? Former Anakim, latter Ugallu.<br /> <br /> <br /> Check out pp. 40-43 of the BPG, it gives more information on the Family, ideas for possibly Horrors (from the almost-too-human to the Slenderman to the &quot;Looks normal, except for those pitch-black eyes&quot; to 'scramble his limbs around a bit', additional limbs etc. It even mentions mirrorskin-like Horrors.), how they approach Kinships etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T03:41:06-08:00","id":1193481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193453#post1193453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combaining those two responses - <b>So Family in BtP, in the end, is only 'Color' of PC? </b>The same archetype of Horror can easily by Inguma, Namtaru or Makara, depending only on players choice?<br /> <br /> <b>So what are most striking traits of Inguma on their own? 'Subversiveness' of community?</b> For example - Does ethnic mythological being inside the human body of the same ethnicity <i>is not</i> Inguma, as it's too much 'in the open'? First Nation Horror inside First Nation human is too much counter to Inguma inborn 'stealthiness' inside population? Would Dybbuk inside Jew person is not good for Inguma Family?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see now that was a poor choice of words on my part.<br /> <br /> As for the Inguma on their own; they support a very paranoid style. If done right, you are afraid of them because they could be anyone, because you can't understand them. As far as subversiveness goes, matching Horror to ethnicity is not an issue for how I see them; people will always subdivided their groups. It doesn't matter if they are both from the First Nations (who, I assume, are the 'Natives' you have over there in the U.S.) because they could be from another tribe or from a family with a vendetta or 'corrupted', etc.<br /> <br /> Inguma are not just the Other. They are the neighbour, they could be anyone, but they are not like you. That is what the Family brings to the table","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T09:33:32-08:00","id":1193596,"title":"","content":"Amusingly the T-1000 in wasn't originally meant to the unstoppable killer type that fits the Anakim archetype. Before they cast Arnold the guy they had planned had looked really plain and the idea was literally going to be an inability to find out who it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:45:03-08:00","id":1193622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193596#post1193596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amusingly the T-1000 in wasn't originally meant to the unstoppable killer type that fits the Anakim archetype. Before they cast Arnold the guy they had planned had looked really plain and the idea was literally going to be an inability to find out who it was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the T-800.<br /> <br /> The T-1000 (played by Robert Patrick) actually does have the can't tell who it is thing going on with the shape-shifting (although also the unstoppable thing). Seems like they decided to use the original idea in the second movie (sort of).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:50:21-08:00","id":1193626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193622#post1193622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's the T-800.<br /> <br /> The T-1000 (played by Robert Patrick) actually does have the can't tell who it is thing going on with the shape-shifting (although also the unstoppable thing). Seems like they decided to use the original idea in the second movie (sort of).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right right ,I get the number mixed up sometimes. Probably doesn't help that I don't normally even refer to the different film terminators by number. Though as you say it does still fit that anakim/inugami dichotomy since the thing is either something you can't tell who it is, or you play up the part where it repeatedly shrugged off having holes punched through it for an Anakim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-09-2018, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:53:14-08:00","id":1193628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193626#post1193626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right right ,I get the number mixed up sometimes. Probably doesn't help that I don't normally even refer to the different film terminator's by number. Though as you say it does still fit that anakim inugami dichotomy since the thing is either something you can't tell who it is, or you play up the part where it repeatedly shrugged off having holes punched through it for an Anakim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Terminator is actually a pretty good source for Beast inspiration. Inugami just make it better with the T-1000.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T04:23:48-07:00","id":1212593,"title":"","content":"Question - As I'm clearly on inclusion of LGBT+ characters all over the <b>CoD</b> ( and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-wod-games\">it's not that hard right now</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I have a question on recreating one of most cool 2E powers added to Uratha - <i>Luna's Embrace</i>, i.e. sex changing power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If changing oneself in to other sex version ( male Inguma into female self, female Beast into male self ) would be variant of <i>Enemy Within</i> Atavism, in it's normal usage. Or you need to use some extra power to make it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-28-2018, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:47:55-07:00","id":1212612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1212593#post1212593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question - As I'm clearly on inclusion of LGBT+ characters all over the <b>CoD</b> ( and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-wod-games\">it's not that hard right now</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I have a question on recreating one of most cool 2E powers added to Uratha - <i>Luna's Embrace</i>, i.e. sex changing power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If changing oneself in to other sex version ( male Inguma into female self, female Beast into male self ) would be variant of <i>Enemy Within</i> Atavism, in it's normal usage. Or you need to use some extra power to make it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can certainly disguise yourself as someone of the opposite sex, but actually changing your gender into a shape that isn't someone else's? Not sure. It does sound like an excellent idea for a Werewolf or Mage Kinship merit, possibly with Enemy Within as a prerequisite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:44:36-07:00","id":1212635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1212593#post1212593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question - As I'm clearly on inclusion of LGBT+ characters all over the <b>CoD</b> ( and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-wod-games\">it's not that hard right now</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I have a question on recreating one of most cool 2E powers added to Uratha - <i>Luna's Embrace</i>, i.e. sex changing power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If changing oneself in to other sex version ( male Inguma into female self, female Beast into male self ) would be variant of <i>Enemy Within</i> Atavism, in it's normal usage. Or you need to use some extra power to make it work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An actual physical change, as opposed to a disguise? Sounds like a Birthright or a Merit. Enemy Within mimics a specific victim, so not sure if that'd be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T13:41:39-07:00","id":1212781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1212612#post1212612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does sound like an excellent idea for a Werewolf or Mage Kinship merit, possibly with Enemy Within as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, how this would work like? As fan stuff, I take a bit liberty adding to whole Inguma Family as alternative Prerequisite to Merit - as it sounds as perfect fit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Shed a Skin (**?)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Inguma Family OR Family Ties with a werewolves or Life mages<br /> Inguma Family is known for being Nightmares of Other. One of greatest horrors to men is awaking in the skin of women - and vice versa. By taping into those fears - or being inspired for shapechanging abilities of werewolves and some mages - Beast can assume once own physical sex change, i.e. male Begotten become female version of his own body, or female Child of Dark Mother become male version of her own body. Change follows rules of <i>Enemy </i><i>Within</i> Atavism on Satiety Expenditure ( see <b>Beast Player's Guide</b>, page 84 ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T00:17:15-07:00","id":1212969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1212781#post1212781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, how this would work like? As fan stuff, I take a bit liberty adding to whole Inguma Family as alternative Prerequisite to Merit - as it sounds as perfect fit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Shed a Skin (**?)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Inguma Family OR Family Ties with a werewolves or Life mages<br /> Inguma Family is known for being Nightmares of Other. One of greatest horrors to men is awaking in the skin of women - and vice versa. By taping into those fears - or being inspired for shapechanging abilities of werewolves and some mages - Beast can assume once own physical sex change, i.e. male Begotten become female version of his own body, or female Child of Dark Mother become male version of her own body. Change follows rules of <i>Enemy </i><i>Within</i> Atavism on Satiety Expenditure ( see <b>Beast Player's Guide</b>, page 84 ).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to do it, I think I'd probably do it more like this:<br /> <br /> <u><b>A Foot in Both Worlds (OOO)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Werewolf kinship <i>or</i> Life Mage kinship <i>or</i> Enemy Within Atavism <i>or</i> Inguma Family<br /> Perhaps the fundamental division within humanity is that between the sexes, but many are the monsters who transgress upon this boundary - half-man, half-woman things, shapeshifters, illusionists and altogether stranger things. A Beast with this Merit can do likewise, spending two points of Willpower to transform into the opposite sex, a hermaphrodite or a genderless androgyne until Second Self is used again. The change is biologically complete and functional, and the Beast appears as if they were a sibling of the new gender. The change lasts until Second Self is used again to change back. Some Beasts who possess this Merit use it as a form of disguise (it's a rare pursuer who'll think that a woman who looks like the man he was chasing <i>is </i>that person), but it is also a godsend - or a gift from the Dark Mother - to transgender or gender-nonbinary Begotten.<br /> <div align=\"center\">XxXxX</div> <br /> The hermaphrodite and androgyne options are for the sake of adding an extra element of uncomfortableness when 'normal' people encounter a Beast with this Merit. After all, Beasts are creatures of fear and myth, and I don't think that any Beast-specific supernatural Merit should be entirely divorced from the nature of the Horror and the Dark Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-01-2018, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T05:43:11-07:00","id":1213022,"title":"","content":"Excelent stuff, <b>ajf</b>! I would only point in here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1212969#post1212969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>A Foot in Both Worlds (OOO)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Werewolf kinship <i>or</i> Life Mage kinship <i>or</i> Enemy Within <i>or</i> Inguma Family</div> </div> </div> </div>... that <i>Enemy Within</i> is Atavism - in other prerequisites you pointed all the parts of mechanics they are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T04:39:36-07:00","id":1214106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193235#post1193235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather <i>all </i>minorities groups - Queer are just most interesting topic as we do not have many myths about them as Fears engines, compared to whole mythologies of ethnics groups ( like Jews, for example ). Still, you are welcome here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> It doesn't have to be a minority, everybody is &quot;other&quot; to somebody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T07:12:51-07:00","id":1214145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1214106#post1214106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't have to be a minority, everybody is &quot;other&quot; to somebody.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that from Inguma stand point, to be 'The Other' you need to have some distinctive features, however good they are hidden. Your faith ( in West Judaism or Islam, for example ), your skin color, orientation or gender identity. In small communities - like are many in modern Poland - it maybe <i>very hard</i> to found <b>someone</b> that is 'other' to subvert those standards. We - officially - are nation of white straight Catholics. And in small town or village communities - it very much feel that way. Every one is like made from template of 'Pole-Catholic'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:28:45-07:00","id":1214171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1214145#post1214145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would argue that from Inguma stand point, to be 'The Other' you need to have some distinctive features, however good they are hidden. Your faith ( in West Judaism or Islam, for example ), your skin color, orientation or gender identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to read Inguma, yes, but it doesn't have to be the only way. Inguma could also easily represent the fear of hostile takeover of a business or political party, someone that hides in plain sight until it is too late for you to do anything about it (and yes, there are other families that idea could work for as well, but Inguma is one of them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:36:45-07:00","id":1214174,"title":"","content":"You are probably right - I remember great 'He is communist!' Horror made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12970_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12970\" data-vbnamecard=\"12970\">Gellydog</a> in other topic that is also Inguma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1199451-how-do-you-create-a-horror?p=1199478#post1199478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Red Specter</b></span><br /> <br /> A Horror inspired by the fears of Communist infiltration and nuclear annihilation that were rampant during the Cold War, the Red Specter is a nightmare of paranoia, foreign influence, unfamiliar and frightening ideologies, world-ending threats and the fragility of &quot;civilized&quot; society. It reminds us that no matter how advanced we think we are, at heart we're still animals huddling together in packs, fearing those who believe and act differently. And that in our desperation to keep &quot;them&quot; away from &quot;us,&quot; we could easily destroy everything we've ever loved...<br /> <br /> So, this idea immediately suggests Inguma as a Family: Nightmares of the Other fits pretty exactly into what we're looking for with &quot;the Reds are infiltrating our society.&quot; The Outsiders have plenty of nice Atavisms that can create paranoia and distrust, and we can fill out from other Families as needed. Speaking of Atavisms, I'd say we could start (I always begin with a character at &quot;just created,&quot; then advance them as needed) with Enemy Within and Touch of the Basilisk. Enemy Within is a perfect fit for an infiltrator and subversive; it lets you take on other people's identities, and fulfills our &quot;at least one in-Family&quot; requirement at character creation. Basilisk's Touch is more out-there, but in this case I'd say we fashion it as radiation sickness. The Red Specter is an embodiment of Red Scare fears, and the &quot;threat&quot; of Communism wasn't simply that it was different; it was that the Reds had nuclear weapons...and how can we be safe while <i>their kind</i> have such power? A future addition would be Alien Mindset; those dirty Reds don't even <i>think</i> like us, don't you know!?<br /> <br /> So we've established that the Red Specter represents both the subtle fear of subversion and the existential terror of armageddon. I think for a Lair, we should focus on showing the ultimate end of those fears. The Heart Chamber takes the form of a familiar city, but after the bombs have fallen. It's a blasted-out ruin, irradiated and lifeless, red dust choking the sky and smoke burning the eyes. I don't have my core book with me, but I'm sure there are traits that could represent the rubble everywhere and the fallout from the blasts. (in which case, any sort of ruined or abandoned structure would be a great place for the Beast to make a stand, given that resonance would allow them to flood the place with deadly radiation... &gt;:3) Future Chambers could continue the theme, adding traits to represent choking smoke, oppressive heat and unstable ground. (if you wanted to get <i>really</i> weird, add Minions or Thralls and summon some mutants!)<br /> <br /> For the Horror's physical form, and say a gaunt and skeletal human figure wearing a tattered, nondescript military uniform. Its skin is loose and burned, and its clothes are tatted and hanging off its frame. A grim death's-head makes up its face, with only two horribly glowing eyes (a sickly green) looking alive.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Hunger. There's a few you could go with- Ruin, for the apocalyptic threat; Hoard, as you &quot;collect&quot; &quot;converts&quot;; or Punishment, targeting those who believe &quot;wrong.&quot; Ultimately, though, I definitely want to go with Transgression- the Red Specter feeds off betrayal, when people knowingly break with their professed beliefs. This fits well with the idea of subversion that the &quot;Communist threat&quot; was supposed to represent. &quot;They&quot; were infiltrating our society and poisoning our minds with their evil ideology; even our most cherished institutions and leaders could be turned against us. Communism often was treated as this sort of thought virus, where even <i>learning</i> about it would turn pure, innocent Americans into drones who would sell out their friends, family and country.<br /> <br /> So, we take that and run with it- the Horror wants to see people turn against whatever it is that they hold most dear. At low satiety, it will be enough to convince a victim to blow off a dinner date or sleep through a doctor's appointment. At high levels, they need to knowingly and willfully betray a person or organization they hold allegiance to. They don't need to get caught, or suffer consequences- they just need to <i>know</i> that they've committed a betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:50:34-07:00","id":1214177,"title":"","content":"I just wonder how to represent Fear of Jews and Muslims in 15th century Iberia? What, make Horrors looks like Dybbuk or Jinn - or use satirical, xenophobic illustrations of those minorities?<br /> <br /> <b>Notice:</b> Offending picture of antisemitism origin.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://s19453.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/the_happy_merchant_by_567a45-d6lbzsg-405x580.jpghttp://s19453.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/the_happy_merchant_by_567a45-d6lbzsg-405x580.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://s19453.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/the_happy_merchant_by_567a45-d6lbzsg-405x580.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:53:02-07:00","id":1214179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1214177#post1214177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wonder how to represent Fear of Jews and Muslims in 15th century Iberia? What, make Horrors looks like Dybbuk or Jinn - or use satirical, xenophobic illustrations of those minorities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would go with the former rather than the later. There are some nasty implications if you xenophobic images as the Horrors themselves and it could very easily become offensive and uncomfortable in an unintended way for someone at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:53:03-07:00","id":1214218,"title":"","content":"Dybbuk is in Judaism mostly name for the typical ghost that posses Jews. As very ghost-like it clearly would be Eshmaki Family - but as I understand game, the same Horror can also be Inguma, if the way it's interacting with his victims is based more on Fear of Other in community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T06:01:11-07:00","id":1215008,"title":"","content":"&quot;He stands Tall, perhaps a bit too tall, something is off about him but you can't tell what. He looks just like everyone else, the same as you. You know you've seen him around many times, but only now do you feel it, something is wrong with him... Then he smiles down at you and the world twists. His <i>Eyes</i>... Why are they black.....&quot;<br /> <br /> The Other doesn't even need to mean a Minority just the FEAR of one. the Fear that something you know is suddenly pulled away and you see it. Everything is the same... But the other has always been there.<br /> <br /> I've probably rambled... and made no sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:45:21-07:00","id":1215051,"title":"","content":"For Jews, there's the myth that they grow horns during their religious ceremonies. That could be worked into a Horror's description.<br /> <br /> For some more inspiration about &quot;infiltrating&quot; a community and &quot;corrupting&quot; it, Cronenberg's <i>Shivers</i> has some. A man develops a parasite that makes everyone into raging sex fiends and/or violent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:09:52-07:00","id":1216098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1215051#post1215051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Jews, there's the myth that they grow horns during their religious ceremonies. That could be worked into a Horror's description.<br /> <br /> For some more inspiration about &quot;infiltrating&quot; a community and &quot;corrupting&quot; it, Cronenberg's <i>Shivers</i> has some. A man develops a parasite that makes everyone into raging sex fiends and/or violent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had an idea for a Horror inspired by the Hykos Dynasies in Egypt, with the Beast who goes by the name Apopis (after the last Hykos Pharoah) coming off as a different minority to everyone. To Jews he'd look Palestian, to Arabs he'd look abit Jewish, to whites he'd look like a light skinned black person, to black people he'd look greek or Italian.<br /> <br /> his horror would be Ba'al Set, a fusion of the Canaanite Ba'al and the Egyptian Set who became linked to the idea of Hykos and rule by outsiders. Ba'al Set would look like a giant Pharaoh with reptialian features. Family: Inguma, Hunger: Hunger for Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T10:39:02-07:00","id":1217711,"title":"","content":"Just got idea for ma\u0142e Inguma Tempter who seducess priests to sex with him, and breaking their vows of chastity, with bonus points for engaging in same sex physical actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T06:12:58-07:00","id":1217947,"title":"","content":"Another take on Inguma might be based on ritual or cultural impurities. Things that temporarily or permanently remove a person from their normal community. Working with dead flesh is a common one - perhaps the Horror resembles a leather-clad, bloodstained individual, wielding butcher's or tanner's tools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193460#post1193460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inguma are the Fear of the Other, Makara the Fear of Drowning and Namtaru the Fear of Revulsion. The same Archetype of Horror can easily be either of those, depending on where you put your focus. Is it more about fearing something because it is different, or because it makes you gag? Former Inguma, later Namtaru.</div> </div> </div> </div>From that perspective, what about the immigrant's fear of a host community that may be a hair's-breadth from turning on them? (For a lot of Eastern Europeans in the UK that's a pretty rational fear). Would you make that Inguma because it's other people, even if they're majority this time, or Makara because they represent an environment that can crush you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1214218#post1214218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dybbuk is in Judaism mostly name for the typical ghost that posses Jews. As very ghost-like it clearly would be Eshmaki Family - but as I understand game, the same Horror can also be Inguma, if the way it's interacting with his victims is based more on Fear of Other in community.</div> </div> </div> </div>Connecting a dybbuk to the Inguma needn't represent gentiles' othering of Jews, but Jews' othering of the possessed - the dybbuk's possession presumably causes proclivities that take its victim outside the norms of the community - which can then be a both an internal and external fear for the victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T13:09:14-07:00","id":1218046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities#post1193199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I have real problem in imaging how could look like Horror reflecting fears about LGBT+ people</b> - What, this being would look like mismatched amalgam of male and women parts? Or something like <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Slaanesh\" target=\"_blank\">Warhammer\u2019s Slaanesh</a>? Because \u2018man dressed as women\u2019 is clearly not enough as true Horror image.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Might wanna tread carefully around this subject.<br /> <br /> I once wrote up an Inguma Enabler who's preferred feeding method was exposing hypocrites, such as closet homosexuals who abused the openly gay, and almost ended up with a permanent ban. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But to answer the question, I believe that in order to sell the aspect of terror this family is supposed to embody, they would be expected to feature exaggerated versions of offensive stereotypes.<br /> <br /> They have to give people a reason to want them kicked out, after all. That's not something you accomplish by just showing up on scene and acting like a normal person.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Inguma are probably going to be the most sensitive characters in the game, even if their family is appropriate for the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T15:18:14-07:00","id":1218072,"title":"","content":"<b>Sorry for the double post.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1193453#post1193453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Combaining those two responses - <b>So Family in BtP, in the end, is only 'Color' of PC? </b>The same archetype of Horror can easily by Inguma, Namtaru or Makara, depending only on players choice?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, yes. You don't have to be an Inguma to represent minority groups, but the different families might represent them in different ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Makara are fear of the depths, which I personally like to interpret as being dumped into an environment you are unaccustomed to. So instead of being the minority facing off against the threat of the majority, you pluck a member of the majority and drop them in an area where the minority holds sway over things. Now the roles are reversed, with the (former) majority finding themselves surrounded on all sides by the very thing they fear, and they probably start freaking out because of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure how to differentiate Inguma minorities from Namtaru minorities, other than to suggest that the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Inguma are simply going about their affairs as normal, while the </span></span></span>Namtaru openly flaunt their differences around others.<br /> <br /> <br /> One family represents minorities going about their daily lives and facing prejudice because of it. The other family represents minorities actively encouraging prejudice based on their their public displays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-12-2018, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}